    "notes": "Single melody part. Verse section (bars 1-8): four stacked lines, lyric numbers 1-4. Refrain (bars 9-20): text printed ONCE on the first line and sung after every stanza; truth encodes it only as lyric number 1 (lyric/@name=\"refrain\"); lines 2-4 have no syllables in the refrain. \"Glo-\" is held over a 16-note melisma (hyphen, syllabic begin, no extend). Stanza 4 has an elision \"dre‿hom\" (two syllables on one note: <elision>). French punctuation is preceded by a no-break space (U+00A0) exactly as printed; a lenient scorer may normalise whitespace. scan-severe.pdf is a phone photo rotated 90 degrees.",
